1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,070
Breda: Hello, Wayside Camera Club, Breda speaking.

2
00:00:04,070 --> 00:00:06,560
Dan: Oh, hello, um, my name's Dan

3
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:10,499
and I'd like to join your club. Breda: That's great, Dan.

4
00:00:10,499 --> 00:00:12,030
We have an application form -

5
00:00:12,030 --> 00:00:14,700
would you like to complete it over the phone

6
00:00:15,120 --> 00:00:17,540
then you can ask any questions you might have?

7
00:00:17,540 --> 00:00:18,770
Dan: Oh, yes, thanks.

8
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:22,280
Breda: OK, so what's your family name?

9
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:24,750
Dan: It's Green - Dan Green.

10
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:27,620
Breda: So - can I take your email address?

11
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:34,820
Dan: Yes, it's dan1068@market. com.

12
00:00:34,820 --> 00:00:38,830
Breda: Thanks. And what about your home address?

13
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:43,860
Dan: Well, I'm about ten miles away from your club in Peacetown

14
00:00:44,240 --> 00:00:45,790
I live in a house there.

15
00:00:45,790 --> 00:00:49,500
Breda: OK, so what's the house number and street?

16
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:53,340
Dan: It's 52 Marrowfield Street.

17
00:00:53,340 --> 00:01:04,570
Breda: Is that M-A double R-O-W-F-I-E-L-D?

18
00:01:04,570 --> 00:01:05,830
Dan: That's right.

19
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:08,510
Breda:... and that's Peacetown, you said?

20
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:14,140
Dan: Uhuh. Breda: So how did you hear about our club? Did you look on the internet?

21
00:01:14,140 --> 00:01:17,280
Dan: I usually do that, but this time

22
00:01:17,860 --> 00:01:22,580
well, I was talking to a relative the other day and he suggested it.

23
00:01:22,580 --> 00:01:24,990
Breda: Oh, is he a member too?

24
00:01:24,990 --> 00:01:29,770
Dan: He belongs to another club - but he'd heard good things about yours.

25
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:34,070
Breda: OK. So what do you hope to get from joining?

26
00:01:34,070 --> 00:01:41,920
Dan: Well, one thing that really interests me is the competitions that you have. I enjoy entering those.

27
00:01:41,920 --> 00:01:44,220
Breda: Right. Anything else?

28
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:48,290
Dan: Well, I also like to socialise with other photographers.

29
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:52,660
Breda: That's great. So what type of membership would you like?

30
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:54,430
Dan: What are the options?

31
00:01:54,430 --> 00:02:01,070
Breda: It's £30 a year for full membership or £20 a year if you're an associate.

32
00:02:01,070 --> 00:02:04,790
Dan: I think I'll go for the full membership, then.

33
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:06,500
Breda: That's a good idea

34
00:02:06,840 --> 00:02:12,570
because you can't vote in meetings with an associate membership.

35
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:15,710
Breda: If I could just find out a bit more about you...

36
00:02:15,710 --> 00:02:16,510
Dan: OK.

37
00:02:16,510 --> 00:02:19,400
Breda: So you said you wanted to compete

38
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,010
have you ever won any photography competitions?

39
00:02:23,010 --> 00:02:27,410
Dan: Not yet, but I have entered three in the past.

40
00:02:27,410 --> 00:02:32,440
Breda: Oh, that's interesting. So why don't you tell me something about those

41
00:02:32,820 --> 00:02:34,880
Let's start with the first one.

42
00:02:34,880 --> 00:02:39,280
Dan: Well, the theme was entitled 'Domestic Life'.

43
00:02:39,280 --> 00:02:43,700
Breda: I see - so it had to be something related to the home?

44
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:51,306
Dan: Yeah. I chose to take a photo of a family sitting round the dinner table having a meal,

45
00:02:51,306 --> 00:02:56,110
and, um, I didn't win, but I did get some feedback.

46
00:02:56,110 --> 00:02:58,520
Breda: Oh, what did the judges say?

47
00:02:58,520 --> 00:03:01,380
Dan: That it was too 'busy' as a picture.

48
00:03:01,380 --> 00:03:06,980
Breda: Aha - so it was the composition of the picture that they criticised?

49
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:12,710
Dan: That's right - and once they'd told me that, I could see my mistake.

50
00:03:12,710 --> 00:03:16,210
Breda: So what was the theme of the second competition?

51
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:19,300
Dan: Well, my university was on the coast

52
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:23,100
and that area gets a lot of beautiful sunsets

53
00:03:23,540 --> 00:03:25,330
so that was the theme.

54
00:03:25,330 --> 00:03:28,870
Breda: Oh, sunsets, that's a great theme.

55
00:03:28,870 --> 00:03:33,500
Dan: Yes. The instructions were to capture the clouds as well

56
00:03:33,880 --> 00:03:37,270
it couldn't just be blue sky and a setting sun.

57
00:03:37,270 --> 00:03:41,580
Breda: Sure, cause they give you all those amazing pinks and purples.

58
00:03:41,580 --> 00:03:44,849
Dan: Yeah - and I thought I'd done that well,

59
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:50,080
but the feedback was that I should have waited a bit longer to get the shot.

60
00:03:50,080 --> 00:03:54,520
Breda: I see. So the timing wasn't right.

61
00:03:54,520 --> 00:03:56,560
Dan: Yes - I took it too soon, basically

62
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:02,280
And then the third competition I entered was called 'Animal Magic'.

63
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:04,980
Breda: Well, that's a difficult subject!

64
00:04:04,980 --> 00:04:08,880
Dan: I know! I had to take hundreds of shots.

65
00:04:08,880 --> 00:04:12,380
Breda: I'm sure - because animals move all the time.

66
00:04:12,380 --> 00:04:18,187
Dan: That's what we had to show - there had to be some movement in the scene.

67
00:04:18,187 --> 00:04:21,945
I got a great shot of a fox in the end,

68
00:04:21,945 --> 00:04:24,660
but I took it at night and, well

69
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:29,460
I suspected that it was a bit dark, which is what I was told.

70
00:04:29,460 --> 00:04:32,620
Breda: Well Dan - you seem to be really keen

71
00:04:32,620 --> 00:04:35,495
and we'd be delighted to have you in our club.

72
00:04:35,495 --> 00:04:39,720
I'm sure we can help with all those areas that you've outlined.

73
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,630
Dan: Thanks, that's great.
